# Basic OSPF Configuration

R2:

router ospf 1
 router-id 2.2.2.2
 network 10.23.23.0 0.0.0.3 area 0


R3:

router ospf 1
 router-id 3.3.3.3
 network 10.23.23.0 0.0.0.3 area 0


# Passive Interfaces

VLAN and loopback interfaces can be made passive when they should
advertise their networks but should not form OSPF adjacencies.

Example:

router ospf 1
 passive-interface loopback1


# OSPF Authentication

Example:

interface GigabitEthernet0/0
 ip ospf authentication message-digest
 ip ospf message-digest-key 1 md5 CCNP


# OSPF Area Summarization

ABR summarization example:

router ospf 1
 area 10 range 10.10.0.0 255.255.0.0


# Default Route

Example:

ip route 0.0.0.0 0.0.0.0 <next-hop>

router ospf 1
 default-information originate


# Stub Area

router ospf 1
 area 10 stub


# Totally Stubby Area

router ospf 1
 area 10 stub no-summary


# NSSA

router ospf 1
 area 10 nssa


# NSSA Totally Stubby

router ospf 1
 area 10 nssa no-summary


